steps.text:
Use custom keybindings that pass `logicalLine: true` to the cursor commands:

```json
[
  {
    "key": "ctrl+alt+down",
    "command": "editor.action.insertCursorBelow",
    "args": { "logicalLine": true }
  },
  {
    "key": "ctrl+alt+up",
    "command": "editor.action.insertCursorAbove",
    "args": { "logicalLine": true }
  }
]
```

On macOS, replace `ctrl` with `cmd` if desired. This makes Add Cursor Above/Below move by real document lines, ignoring visual word-wrap continuations—the behavior in your second GIF.
